<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The endpoint config and the entry module, for the pages that can actually show a card.

  **Why a handle of its own rather than `default`.** These two tags used to render on every page —
  the cart, the checkout, the login form, every CMS page — because the block was declared in the
  module's `default.xml`. Nothing on those pages reads either one.

  **Why not `catalog_list_item`, where the renderer lives.** That handle is included from `default`
  whenever Page Builder is installed, which is most storefronts, so declaring the scripts there
  would put them straight back on every page.

  **Why still in the head, and not gated on a card having rendered.** Hyvä's `BlockJsDependencies`
  renders a dependency from `before.body.end`, and `<script type="module">` is deferred: deferred
  scripts execute in document order, so an entry module rendered after Hyvä's Alpine tag runs after
  Alpine has already walked the DOM. That was tried, and every card on the page reported
  `scr1beProductCard is not defined`. In the head it is ahead of Alpine, which is the whole
  requirement.

  A product-list widget dropped on a page outside these handles still renders its cards server-side;
  it just arrives without the interactive layer. Opt that page in by adding its handle here.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceContainer name="head.additional">
            <block class="Scr1be\HyvaProductCard\Block\CardScripts"
                   name="scr1be.product.card.scripts"
                   template="Scr1be_HyvaProductCard::product/card/scripts.phtml"/>
        </referenceContainer>
    </body>
</page>
